	abstract = {Various properties essential to the understanding of Stokes flow are discussed, including reversibility, negligibility of inertial forces and minimum energy dissipation theorem. Illustrative examples related to these properties are provided: inertial terms for the fluid flow generated by a rotating cylinder, force on a rotating cylinder close to a solid plane wall, Stokes paradox, energy dissipation for particles of different shapes. The meaning and the limits of the Stokes approximation are discussed in the context of more general equations.},
